      "id": "PC-OT-001",
      "title": "Cyber-Informed Engineering",
      "status": "draft",
      "description": "DRAFT. The capability to apply Cyber-Informed Engineering (CIE): using engineering design, not only added security controls, to eliminate or limit the consequences a cyber attack on an industrial system could cause, across the whole system lifecycle. Organized by the 12 CIE principles in DOE's National CIE Strategy and INL's CIE Implementation Guide. CIE is aimed at the engineers and technicians who design, build, operate and maintain physical infrastructure, not only at cybersecurity specialists.",
